      "body": "## Overview\nCollect NIXL pull block IDs and per-group cached-block counts in one admission traversal, using the existing null-prefix trimming helper.\n\n## Claims\nPreserve interior-null filtering, interleaved hashes, DCP offsets, transfer-group clipping and empty transfers for full local hits. Reduce scheduler CPU work; no end-to-end throughput or TTFT gain is claimed.\n\n## Validation\nHead `1e88d2077`, base `4b1c04e76`; production code is unchanged. Current four-file CPU selection: **494 passed**, 169 deselected. The existing per-group regression now covers a long null prefix and no-transfer admission with real scheduler construction. Whole-diff pre-commit including mypy passed.\n\n```bash\nHF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' \\\nuv run --no-project .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -m cpu_test \\\n  tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_nixl_connector.py \\\n  tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_nixl_connector_hma.py \\\n  tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_nixl_desc_geometry.py \\\n  tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py\n```\n\nEarlier CPython 3.12 admission microbenchmark: 100 warmups, 8 alternating rounds, 400 calls/long case. A 128K-equivalent layout (1,000 hashed full-attention blocks plus eight null-prefixed sliding-window groups) measured **1,609 → 153 µs** for the complete admission callback; 32K measured **431 → 50 µs**. Production matches that measurement. Earlier differential and synthetic NIXL P/D correctness checks passed; no fresh GPU/performance run this round.\n\n## Details\nD allocates blocks, this callback produces pull IDs and cached counts, then the existing transfer/release protocol runs. No persistent cache or switch is added. This follows merged #61724; #55374 addresses piecewise loading. AI assistance was used for implementation and validation.\n\n---\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] Design Fit\n- [x] Testing and Validation (scope and gaps above)\n- [x] Code Quality and Style\n- [x] Pull Request Contents\n\n</details>\n",
